+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional :rst:dir:option:`canonical` option
+   gives the alias expression, which is parsed as a Python annotation. Type
+   aliases can be documented at module level or inside a class. The directive
+   body can describe the alias.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical: alias expression
+      :type: text
+
+      The expression assigned to the alias. Names in the expression are parsed
+      as Python type references.
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: module
+      :type: text
+
+      Describe the location where the object is defined. The default value is
+      the module specified by :rst:dir:`py:currentmodule`.
+
